    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-4271",
      "problem": "Consider a vector $\\textbf{a}$ and a point $O$ (shown below). Draw a vector that is equal to the vector $\\textbf{a}$ and has its tail at $O.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14196310/assets/571e2d2a8ffab997a13f99973a8605c5b9b410439239a3acef5a7fd1dac939ae.png)",
      "worked_solution": "First, we sketch the line that is passing through $O$ and parallel to $\\textbf{a}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14196310/assets/1c1acea46337104f17184784dfc9fecc21360112fc510ac56665565e1c800804.png)\n\nNow, we choose a point $B$ on the line, in the direction of $\\textbf{a},$ such that $OB$ equals the length of $\\textbf{a}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14196310/assets/0931711b7da5d109085f729999016f0b7c7fb7930f658a909739910c37d05ce8.png)\n\nSo, the vector $\\overrightarrow{OB}$ is equal to the vector $\\textbf{a}$ and has its tail at $O.$",
